From e8914e477b2b3777728053d7945be5bc22cfb427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:41:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Keep typed operational target failures pending during
 recovery

Add a separate immutable reference-generated coinbase-funded fork fixture without modifying existing golden bytes. The existing development profile is unchanged except for an explicitly bound local max_steps=1 host guard; source blocks require no VM invocation. Python and ordinary-guard native validation accept both branches.

Check that the authenticated target spend reaches the host-step guard and returns Inconclusive without a DeterministicBlockFailure proof. Retry target attachment across reopen and require identical raw journal bytes, tip, state root, monetary state, touched coin proofs, retained body/history and active index. The supplied progress output stays untouched and durable progress never advances or marks replacement invalid. Retain the existing malformed-middle deterministic restoration regression.

The strict standalone Debug recovery suite passes with typed validation 022932c53 and corrected root downstream adapters f9d2b3fa3. Requires the typed-validation commit and root disk_block/reorg_recovery adapters with Inconclusive propagation. Only the assigned test source changes; no protocol defaults or production paths are edited.
---
